. sg. दृ॑क्षसे, RV.;
inf. दृशे॑ and दृश॑ये, RV.;
द्र॑ष्टुम्, AV. &c.;
ind.p. दृष्ट्वा॑, AV. &c. [MBh. also दृश्य], ˚ट्वाय, RV.;
-दृ॑श्य, RV.;
-दर्शम्, Daś.)
to see, behold, look at, regard, consider, RV.; AV.; ŚBr.; MBh. &c.;
to see i.e. wait on, visit, MBh.; R.;
to see with the mind, learn, understand, MBh.; Kāv. &c.;
to notice, care for, look into, try, examine, Yājñ.; Pañc.;
to see by divine intuition, think or find out, compose, contrive (hymns, rites, &c.), Br.; Nir. ii, 11 :
Pass. दृश्य॑ते (ep. also ˚ति) aor. अद॑र्शि, RV. &c. to be seen, become visible, appear, RV.; AV.; ŚBr.; MBh. &c.;
to be shown or manifested, appear as (इव), prove, Mn.; MBh.; Kāv. &c.:
Caus. P. Ā. दर्शयति, ˚ते, AV. &c.;
 aor. अदीदृशत्, Br.;
 अददर्शत्, Pāṇ. vii, 4, 7, to cause to see or be seen, to show a thing (Ā. esp. of something belonging to one's self) or person (P. and Ā. with or scil. आत्मानम्, also one's self), to (acc. AV. iv, 20, 6; ŚBr. &c.; gen. Mn. iv, 59; MBh. &c.; dat. R. ii, 31, 33; Ragh. &c.; instr. after Ā. refl, Pāṇ. i, 4, 53, Kāś.);
to show = prove, demonstrate, Mn.; MBh.; Kāv. &c.;
to produce (money) i.e. pay, Mn. viii, 155;
 (a witness), 158 :
Desid. Ā. दिदृक्षते (ep. also ˚ति) to wish to see, long for (acc.), RV. iii, 30, 13; ŚBr.; MBh. &c.:
Desid. of Caus. दिदर्शयिषति, to wish to show, Śaṃk.;
 अदिदर्शयिषीत्, Nid. :
Intens. दरीदृश्यते, to be always visible, Bhojapr.;
 दरीदर्ष्टि or दरिदर्ष्टि or दर्द्˚, Pāṇ. vii, 4, 90; 91.
